            "review_text": "RaeTravels\nBrighton, United Kingdom33 contributions\n0\nSuper-cute with inventive food\nFeb 2024 • Solo\nWhat a delightful wee Buddhist vegetarian restaurant this is! A real find.\n\nTucked down an alleyway, stuffed full of tchotchkes, adorned by a placid white poodle, gay-friendly and run by a couple with good English, this is perfect not only for veggies but for anyone with food intolerances/allergies. The guy serving was super-helpful in working out what I could eat, and I enjoyed my meal.\n\nIf I came back, I'd love to see if they could make a low-FODMAP hotpot. I was jealous of the next table's portable induction hob and plate of mixed mushrooms including oyster, king oyster and dried shiitake! 😃\nRead more\nWritten February 22, 2024",
