            "review_title": "Review at Vegetarian food TuLi KuSu",
            "review_text": "DLTT2015\nLondon, United Kingdom1007 contributions\n0\nHumble menu but fresh delicious food!\nFeb 2023 • Friends\nA lovely vegetarian restaurant tucked within an alley way. The restaurant is very cute and has only a few tables. We sat out side in the alley however the tables inside were full around 6pm. It was only tourists visiting. \n\nThe menu had around 10 things to chose from. The dishes were described basically so I wasn’t excited after ordering but don’t be filled the food was great! There were however no prices on the menu. The lady who served and cooked for us!! didn’t speak much English but we used google translate to communicate and she was so helpful in helping me decide on a meal. \n\nI went for the crispy / soft friend noodles with vegetables and added tofu. This was delicious and not what I had expected. It was lovely stir fried veg with rice noodles on a bed of hard crispy noodles which softened as you ate it. So delicious!\nI also had the crispy fresh fried spring rolls. We got 6 which was a good portion. \n\nA great meal! I would very much recommend!\nRead more\nWritten February 20, 2023",
